INT. TAXIDERMY WORKSHOP - NIGHT

Glass eyes in jars. A fox half-stuffed on the bench. Rain on a skylight.

ODALYS VEGA (30s, rain-soaked trench coat, badge on her belt) stands in the doorway. At the bench, a WOMAN in a leather apron sews a pheasant's wing. Her back is turned.

ODALYS
Evening. Sorry about the hour.

STRANGER
Kettle's on. Sit.

Odalys sits on a stool. Looks at the fox. The fox looks back.

ODALYS
I'm looking into a break-in at the museum. Friday night.

STRANGER
Terrible. They never lock the back.

ODALYS
That's what the guard said. Funny, because he said she never left the bench that night either.

STRANGER
Who?

ODALYS
Nobody. Your name?

The woman turns. Warm face. Needle in her teeth.

STRANGER
Ingrid.

She sets down the wing. On the shelf behind her: a small brass key tag. MUSEUM - REAR.

INGRID
Does she take sugar, your guard?

Odalys stands. Her hand drifts to her belt. Ingrid smiles.

ODALYS
Ingrid. Put the needle down.
